			<td class="BodyMain" width="88%" colspan="4" align="left"><font size="2">
			
			<font size=5 class="BodyMainReverse">T</font>he Armigers of Mirth is a cross-virtuality guild dedicated to the exploration
			of taverns, the pursuit fair play, and generally having a good time.
			<hr width=100% align=center>
			
			<font size=5 class="BodyMainReverse">W</font>henever possible, players are required to carry a minimum of two drinks with
			them at all times.  Drinking is a great way to solve in-game problems. 
			Remember, when in doubt about how to resolve a situation, offer the other
			player a drink.
			<hr width=100% align=center>
			
			<font size=5 class="BodyMainReverse">I</font>n virtualities which support the skill, Armigers are required to take up
			brewing.  You need not progress beyond hobbyist levels in the skill, but
			becoming a master brewer is a prized goal among the Armigers.  A Player that
			becomes a Master Brewer will be awarded a personalized shot glass acknowledging
			their illustrious achievement (okay its a virtual shotglass).
			<hr width=100% align=center>

			<font size=5 class="BodyMainReverse">N</font>ever drink alone, unless you're celebrating with a Guild Member or Members
			located too far away for you to reasonably gather together.  Always bring
			enough for everyone when you come to drink.
			<hr width=100% align=center>

			<font size=5 class="BodyMainReverse">W</font>hile we don't require role-playing at all times, we believe that it adds fun
			and flavor to any game and certainly recommend role-playing as much as possible.
			<hr width=100% align=center>

			<font size=5 class="BodyMainReverse">K</font>ill stealing, in virtualities where such a concept applies, will not be
			tolerated.  Your actions reflect on The Guild as a whole, and therefore you
			must act in a manner that won't adversely affect our image and reputation. When
			in doubt, offer the other player a drink.
			<hr width=100% align=center>

			<font size=5 class="BodyMainReverse">B</font>efore selling any major item check with the guild members that are online
			first, another guild member may need or want it.  Guild members should get
			first crack at any such items.  This does not mean you have to give your stuff
			away for free.  We simply ask that you allow fellow Armigers the opportunity to
			pay a fair price for an item before you test the open market.  A drink should
			accompany every trade and transaction (again, assuming the given virtuality
			supports this action) so that a toast may be made to its successful completion.</font></td>
